    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d393-a1">

                <pb facs="0728" n="710" sameAs="frus:frus1946v01/pg710"/>

                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Annex—Translation]</seg>
                </opener>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé of the Soviet Union</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Orekhov</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Acting Secretary of
                            State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1946-12-07">December 7,
                        1946</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: With reference to your note of November 6
                    last, in which it was communicated that the United States of America is ready to
                    place under trusteeship the islands which are under Japanese mandate and for
                    which the United States will be the administering authority, I have the honor to
                    inform you of the following:</p>
                <p>The Soviet Government considers it necessary to study the given question and the
                    “Draft Trusteeship Agreement for the Japanese Mandated Islands” which was
                    presented by the Government of the United States of America.</p>
                <p>The Soviet Government is prepared to take into account the interests of the
                    United States of America in connection with this question, but at the same time
                    it considers it necessary to express its view that the question of trusteeship
                    over the islands formerly under Japanese mandate, as well as over any Japanese
                    islands, must be considered by the Allied Powers in the peace settlement in
                    regard to Japan.</p>
                <p>Accept, Sir, the assurance of my very high esteem for you.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>F. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Orekhov</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
